// client-money.prisma — invoices, payments, refunds, receipts, trust ledger, write-offs. Owner: Lead B (client money, contracts §8).
// One file per area (DB-SPLIT, studio/DEVELOPING.md): a new module adds its own file here; never edit another area's file without its owner.
//
// FO-7a (P-558, P-559, P-575 (1), P-576, P-599, P-600; BACKLOG row FO-7a rows rev 7, rev 10 part 2, amended by rev 13;
// contracts platform-and-front-office-contracts-2026-11-14.md §2.5, §7 binding (§2.5 trust), §8; requirements AG-06:
// AG-6-1, -4, -19, -44, -46, -59, -60, -61, -63, -69, -76; Code SOR/2022-128 s. 32, s. 33(3), legal reading
// Unconfirmed: no counsel). Schema only: the API is FO-7b (invoices, payments), FO-7t (trust), FO-7r (write-offs),
// FO-7c (card); the "To move" list (AG-6-73) is row FO-7mv. Nothing outside api/src/client-money/ ever writes these
// tables; other modules ask ClientMoneyPort.
//
// * Like the platform and front-office rows, these carry no workspace_id: the firm is the tenant and the demo reset
//   leaves them. firm_id is first in every index but a primary key. A row naming another money row keys on
//   (firm_id, <id>), so it can never point at another firm's row: composite foreign keys, RESTRICT on delete and update.
// * The firm anchor is money_payment_settings (one row per firm, keyed to platform_firm: the one back-relation line on
//   platform.prisma); every other root table keys to it, so a firm's settings row is written before its first money row.
// * Every amount is an integer in minor units (cents), never a float; every row with an amount carries its currency
//   (CAD by default, USD allowed, AG-6-46 rule 3); amounts in two currencies are never added.
// * The bill-to party is a person or a company (FO-1a's fo_person, fo_company): exactly one of person_id, company_id.
//   FO-1a is not on main yet, so they are uuids with no foreign key; FO-1k adds those keys (rows rev 16).
// * No stored status on an invoice or a trust request: status is derived from facts (AG-6-1 rule 7; FO-7b).
// * Rules Prisma cannot say are in the migration (prisma/migrations/<stamp>_fo7a_client_money_tables): numbers are the
//   database's, taken from a per-firm series inside the writing transaction (no gaps, never reused; AG-6-44); an issued
//   invoice is frozen (lines, tax, party, currency, number); insert-only tables refuse update and delete; a trust
//   withdrawal names an issued invoice of the same party and currency; a party's trust balance never goes below zero
//   (running balance kept by the database, serialised per party and currency); one write-off per invoice; credit
//   notes, the write-off and trust paid on an invoice never exceed it; refunds never exceed their payment; nothing
//   goes into trust while trust is off; issue, send, cancel and record times are the database's; a row a check names
//   must be visible to it (never left to the foreign key at the end of the statement). Each holds at READ COMMITTED
//   and REPEATABLE READ (a unique ordinal or a touched row refuses a stale writer).
// * FO-7mv (AG-6-73, -69 rule 2, -70, -77, -48; P-603, P-607 (1); migration <stamp>_fo7mv_move_list): the "To move" list
//   between the trust and operating bank accounts, money_move_batch and money_move_line, with the derived list
//   money_to_move (a view, no stored status). A move never exceeds what its source still holds; money returned to trust
//   while it is moved is refused until the move is undone; only a wrong-account correction of a deposit licenses a
//   wrong-account move. The routes are FO-7t's.
// * FO-7ts part 1 (AG-6-59 §6-§8, AG-6-4 §7 §13, AG-6-19 rule 1, AG-6-69 §7, AG-6-61 rule 7 §7, AG-6-42 §7; migration
//   <stamp>_fo7ts_money_settings): the three-state trust answer (UNANSWERED → YES | NO, YES ⇄ NO, a trigger; trust is
//   on only at YES) replaces trust_enabled; tax registration (needs a tax number), the QST number and "Prices include
//   tax" replace the firm's rate list; "Invoice payments go to" with who and when; BANK_TRANSFER and CARD_TERMINAL;
//   one deposit request per retainer version; a hashed pay link per document; the unsigned-retainer confirmation; and,
//   in a second step (<stamp>_fo7ts_card_terminal_trust, Lead 80 on #2106), CARD_TERMINAL is never received into trust.
// * FO-7ts part 2 (AG-6-60 rules 2-5, 9, AG-6-21 rules 2-3, 5 §7, AG-6-23 rules 1, 4; P-634; migration
//   <stamp>_fo7ts_ledgers): a pre-case → case move is a MOVE_TO_CASE pair on one party that nets to zero, written in one
//   transaction, at most the pre-case balance; money_credit_entry, the credit ledger per holder (a case, or the party)
//   and currency, insert-only, never below zero. Both write under the party lock (money_trust_lock), then any invoice row.
// * FO-7ts part 3 (AG-6-23 rules 2-3 §7, AG-6-4 rule 2 §7, AG-6-68 rule 4 §7, AG-6-30 rules 2, 4; P-634; migration
//   <stamp>_fo7ts_part3): a trust refund's offline details and payee (never by card); the tax treatment per party and per
//   invoice (fixed at issue); another payer's money pays an invoice only as a pick by the writer, with a reason, on one
//   and the same case, never more than the payer holds on it; the newest-issued index.

/// The two currencies a firm may bill in (AG-6-46 rule 3; X-6). Never converted, never added together.
enum MoneyCurrency {
  CAD
  USD
}

/// The firm's own Stripe connected account (contracts §7 §2.5: controller properties; AG-16-14..18).
enum MoneyAccountStatus {
  NOT_CONNECTED
  PENDING
  ACTIVE
  RESTRICTED
  DISCONNECTED
}

/// An invoice line's kind (row FO-7a). A government fee is never taxed (AG-6-4 rule 3).
enum MoneyLineKind {
  FEE
  DISBURSEMENT
  GOVERNMENT_FEE
}

/// How a payment was made (row FO-7a; AG-6-19 rule 1; FO-7ts part 1 adds BANK_TRANSFER and CARD_TERMINAL). CARD is the
/// online card payment only. Neither CARD nor CARD_TERMINAL is ever received into trust (money_payment_card_not_trust;
/// CARD_TERMINAL from FO-7ts part 1's second step, Lead 80 on #2106; P-567 (3)).
enum MoneyPaymentMethod {
  CARD
  E_TRANSFER
  CHEQUE
  WIRE
  CASH
  OTHER
  BANK_TRANSFER
  CARD_TERMINAL
}

/// The Owner's answer to "Do you hold client money in a trust account?" (AG-6-59 §6-§7; FO-7ts part 1): a firm starts
/// UNANSWERED and behaves as trust off until YES; YES and NO may change, never back to UNANSWERED (a trigger).
enum MoneyTrustAnswer {
  UNANSWERED
  YES
  NO
}

/// "Invoice payments go to" (AG-6-69 rule 3, §7; FO-7ts part 1): its rule and route are FO-7b's.
enum MoneyInvoicePaymentsGoTo {
  OPERATING
  TRUST_FIRST
}

/// The account the money actually reached (AG-6-69). Card money goes to OPERATING only: card into trust waits
/// (contracts §7 §2.5).
enum MoneyAccountKind {
  OPERATING
  TRUST
}

/// How a refund goes back: through the card processor or by the firm itself.
enum MoneyRefundRoute {
  CARD
  OFFLINE
}

/// One receipt series for both kinds (AG-6-63 rule 3): a payment receipt names a payment, a trust receipt a deposit.
enum MoneyReceiptKind {
  PAYMENT
  TRUST
}

/// A trust ledger entry (row FO-7a; contracts §7 §2.5). DEPOSIT is +, WITHDRAWAL_TO_INVOICE and REFUND_TO_CLIENT are −,
/// CORRECTION names one withdrawal (+, money returned from it) or one deposit (−, at most the deposit). Money leaves
/// trust only by a withdrawal to an issued invoice or a refund to the client (P-603). Entries are never changed.
/// MOVE_TO_CASE (FO-7ts part 2; AG-6-60 rules 3, 5, 9): a pair on one party, − with no case, + on a case naming the −,
/// in one transaction; it moves nothing out of trust.
enum MoneyTrustEntryKind {
  DEPOSIT
  WITHDRAWAL_TO_INVOICE
  REFUND_TO_CLIENT
  CORRECTION
  MOVE_TO_CASE
}

/// An invoice's tax treatment (AG-6-4 rule 2 §7; R18): per party (money_party_tax_treatment) or per invoice. FO-7g part 2's
/// rules use it; an invoice's is fixed at issue.
enum MoneyTaxTreatment {
  TAXABLE
  ZERO_RATED
  EXEMPT
}

/// A credit ledger entry's kind (FO-7ts part 2; AG-6-21 rules 2-3, 5; AG-6-23 rule 1; Lead 61, ruling 5c): KEPT (+, a
/// payment's extra kept as credit), APPLIED (−, to an invoice of the same holder), REFUNDED (−, paid back), REVERSED
/// (the opposite sign of the KEPT or APPLIED entry it names).
enum MoneyCreditKind {
  KEPT
  APPLIED
  REFUNDED
  REVERSED
}

/// Why a correction of a deposit was made (FO-7mv; B-19 from #1758; Lead 65, P-638): the reversals of AG-6-75 rule 2
/// ("Returned" a bounced cheque, "Recorded by mistake", "Wrong client", OTHER a typed reason; their ledger rules are
/// FO-7a2's) and WRONG_ACCOUNT, money received into trust that belonged in operating (AG-6-69 rule 2): only
/// WRONG_ACCOUNT licenses a move out of trust.
enum MoneyCorrectionKind {
  RETURNED
  RECORDED_BY_MISTAKE
  WRONG_CLIENT
  OTHER
  WRONG_ACCOUNT
}

/// Credited money that had already moved to operating (FO-7a2 rule 2c, P-634 (2)): refunded to the client, or moved back
/// to trust. It is never kept in operating.
enum MoneyOverpaidChoice {
  OVERPAID_REFUND
  OVERPAID_TO_TRUST
}

/// Why an amount must move between the trust and operating bank accounts (AG-6-73 rule 1 (a)-(c); AG-6-73 §7 names them
/// APPLIED, MISMATCH, FEE_COVER).
enum MoneyMoveKind {
  TRUST_APPLIED
  WRONG_ACCOUNT
  CARD_FEE_ON_TRUST
}

enum MoneyMoveDirection {
  TRUST_TO_OPERATING
  OPERATING_TO_TRUST
}

/// The per-firm number series (AG-6-44): INV-, CN-, R- (payment and trust receipts), DR-.
enum MoneySeriesKind {
  INVOICE
  CREDIT_NOTE
  RECEIPT
  TRUST_REQUEST
}

/// A firm's money settings (AG-6-59, AG-6-71, AG-6-4/-45, AG-6-46, AG-6-69): the operating and trust payment-details
/// blocks printed on invoices and trust requests, tax registration and numbers (rates are ExpatReady data, never the
/// firm's: AG-6-4 §13), the trust answer with who and when (trust off until YES), "Invoice payments go to" with who
/// and when, and the default due period. The firm anchor of this module: one row per firm.
model MoneyPaymentSettings {
  firmId           String        @id @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  operatingDetails String?       @map("operating_details")
  trustDetails     String?       @map("trust_details")
  taxNumber        String?       @map("tax_number")
  /// Registered for tax needs a tax number (a check). Not registered means no tax lines (AG-6-4 rule 5: FO-7g's route); the
/// database does not refuse a tax number kept while not registered (break F6 on facc5231).
  taxRegistered    Boolean       @default(false) @map("tax_registered")
  /// Stored, unused in R1: no Quebec (P-568 (1)).
  qstNumber        String?       @map("qst_number")
  pricesIncludeTax Boolean       @default(false) @map("prices_include_tax")
  /// Who answered is the caller's (the route checks the Owner); when is the database's.
  trustAnswer      MoneyTrustAnswer @default(UNANSWERED) @map("trust_answer")
  trustAnsweredBy  String?          @map("trust_answered_by")
  trustAnsweredAt  DateTime?        @map("trust_answered_at") @db.Timestamptz
  invoicePaymentsGoTo      MoneyInvoicePaymentsGoTo @default(OPERATING) @map("invoice_payments_go_to")
  invoicePaymentsChangedBy String?                  @map("invoice_payments_changed_by")
  invoicePaymentsChangedAt DateTime?                @map("invoice_payments_changed_at") @db.Timestamptz
  defaultCurrency  MoneyCurrency @default(CAD) @map("default_currency")
  dueInDays        Int           @default(14) @map("due_in_days")
  updatedBy        String        @map("updated_by")
  createdAt        DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  updatedAt        DateTime      @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  firm          PlatformFirm         @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  account       MoneyPaymentAccount?
  series        MoneyNumberSeries[]
  invoices      MoneyInvoice[]
  payments      MoneyPayment[]
  trustRequests MoneyTrustRequest[]
  trustEntries  MoneyTrustEntry[]
  moveBatches   MoneyMoveBatch[]
  creditEntries MoneyCreditEntry[]
  partyTaxTreatments MoneyPartyTaxTreatment[]

  @@map("money_payment_settings")
}

/// The firm's own Stripe connected account: its id, status and the two switches Stripe reports (AG-16-14..18). No
/// secret is stored here or anywhere in this module (AG-16-18): the platform's key lives in the secrets loader.
model MoneyPaymentAccount {
  id              String             @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId          String             @unique @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Unique across firms (webhooks are routed by it): the one money_ index without firm_id first.
  stripeAccountId String?            @unique @map("stripe_account_id")
  status          MoneyAccountStatus @default(NOT_CONNECTED)
  chargesEnabled  Boolean            @default(false) @map("charges_enabled")
  payoutsEnabled  Boolean            @default(false) @map("payouts_enabled")
  createdAt       DateTime           @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  updatedAt       DateTime           @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@map("money_payment_account")
}

/// A per-firm number series (AG-6-44): the prefix and the next number. Numbers are taken only by the database
/// (money_take_number, inside the writing transaction), so they never skip or repeat. A firm moving over sets its first
/// number when it writes the row; after that next_number moves only by taking a number. Two series of a firm never
/// share a prefix (letters and a dash).
model MoneyNumberSeries {
  firmId     String          @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  kind       MoneySeriesKind
  prefix     String
  nextNumber Int             @default(1) @map("next_number")
  /// How many numbers the series has given, the database's: while 0, the firm may still set its first number.
  numbersTaken Int @default(0) @map("numbers_taken")
  /// The prefixes this series printed numbers with before its current one, the database's: never another kind's (B-20).
  usedPrefixes String[] @default([]) @map("used_prefixes")
  updatedAt  DateTime        @default(now()) @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@id([firmId, kind])
  @@unique([firmId, prefix])
  @@map("money_number_series")
}

/// An invoice (AG-6-1): on a person or a company (never a prospect), optionally a case. A draft has no number; issuing
/// (issued_at set) takes the next INV- number and freezes the lines, tax, party, currency and number. Status is derived.
model MoneyInvoice {
  id        String        @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId    String        @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  personId  String?       @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId String?       @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  /// The case side's case (runtime_case), when the invoice is on one; no foreign key across the module wall.
  caseId    String?       @map("case_id") @db.Uuid
  number    String?
  currency  MoneyCurrency @default(CAD)
  dueDate   DateTime?     @map("due_date") @db.Date
  issuedAt  DateTime?     @map("issued_at") @db.Timestamptz
  issuedBy  String?       @map("issued_by")
  createdBy String        @map("created_by")
  createdAt DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz
  /// The no-login pay link's SHA-256 in hex, never the token (AG-6-14 rule 3; FO-7ts part 1): unique per firm (a
  /// partial index, in SQL); it may change on an issued invoice (a new link replaces the old one).
  payLinkTokenHash            String?   @map("pay_link_token_hash")
  /// Staff invoiced on an unsigned retainer (AG-6-42 §7: a warning, never a block): both or neither; fixed once issued.
  unsignedRetainerConfirmedBy String?   @map("unsigned_retainer_confirmed_by") @db.Uuid
  unsignedRetainerConfirmedAt DateTime? @map("unsigned_retainer_confirmed_at") @db.Timestamptz
  /// Null on a draft = the party's treatment (money_party_tax_treatment), else Taxable; set to that at issue, then fixed.
  taxTreatment                MoneyTaxTreatment? @map("tax_treatment")
  /// FO-7g part 3 (P-797): the province the tax follows, one of the 13 codes (a CHECK); filled on a new draft from the
  /// client's Canadian address, else the firm's province; editable on a draft; fixed at issue. Null = the firm's province.
  billToProvince              String?            @map("bill_to_province")
  /// FO-7w1: the invoice bills a retainer's "On signing" row, a deposit (Code s. 32; AG-6-61): never a card pay link
  /// (P-567 (3)). Set when the draft is made, fixed after.
  deposit                     Boolean            @default(false)

  settings     MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  lines        MoneyInvoiceLine[]
  creditNotes  MoneyCreditNote[]
  payments     MoneyPayment[]
  trustEntries MoneyTrustEntry[]
  writeOff     MoneyWriteOff?
  moveLines    MoneyMoveLine[]
  creditEntries MoneyCreditEntry[]

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@unique([firmId, number])
  @@index([firmId, personId])
  @@index([firmId, companyId])
  @@index([firmId, caseId])
  @@index([firmId, issuedAt(sort: Desc), id])
  @@map("money_invoice")
}

/// One line of an invoice (AG-6-1 rule 2, AG-6-4): amount = quantity × unit amount; tax rate in parts per million and its
/// amount, rounded per line by FO-7b (within a cent of amount × rate, so two taxes rounded apart fit); a government fee
/// carries no tax.
model MoneyInvoiceLine {
  id              String        @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId          String        @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId       String        @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  position        Int
  kind            MoneyLineKind
  description     String
  quantity        Int           @default(1)
  unitAmountMinor Int           @map("unit_amount_minor")
  amountMinor     Int           @map("amount_minor")
  /// The line's tax rate in parts per million (13 % = 130000; GST + QST 14.975 % = 149750): basis points cannot hold
  /// Quebec's rates (review round 2, Major 1).
  taxRatePpm       Int           @default(0) @map("tax_rate_ppm")
  taxMinor        Int           @default(0) @map("tax_minor")
  currency        MoneyCurrency
  createdAt       DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  /// FO-7w1: the retainer fee row this line bills (fo_retainer_fee_row's id; no foreign key across the module wall).
  /// Unique per firm: a row is billed once; null on a line typed by hand; fixed once written.
  sourceFeeRowId  String?       @map("source_fee_row_id") @db.Uuid

  invoice MoneyInvoice @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, invoiceId, position])
  @@unique([firmId, sourceFeeRowId])
  @@map("money_invoice_line")
}

/// A credit note on an issued invoice (AG-6-48): part or full, with a reason; its CN- number is the database's. The
/// credits on one invoice never exceed its total. Insert-only.
model MoneyCreditNote {
  id          String        @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId      String        @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId   String        @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Always set, by the database when the row is written (a check refuses null); optional here so callers never pass it.
  number      String?
  full        Boolean       @default(false)
  amountMinor Int           @map("amount_minor")
  currency    MoneyCurrency
  reason      String
  /// FO-7a2 rule 2c: for the credited part paid from trust whose money had already moved to operating, the person's
  /// choice, the amount it covers and the trust withdrawal it names (all three or none). OVERPAID_TO_TRUST writes the
  /// return to trust at once and puts an operating → trust line on the To move list.
  overpaidChoice  MoneyOverpaidChoice? @map("overpaid_choice")
  overpaidMinor   Int?                 @map("overpaid_minor")
  overpaidEntryId String?              @map("overpaid_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  createdBy   String        @map("created_by")
  createdAt   DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  invoice       MoneyInvoice     @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  overpaidEntry MoneyTrustEntry? @relation("MoneyCreditNoteOverpaid", fields: [firmId, overpaidEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, number])
  @@index([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@index([firmId, overpaidEntryId])
  @@map("money_credit_note")
}

/// A payment (AG-6-19, AG-6-69): against an issued invoice, a sent trust request, or neither (money with no request,
/// AG-6-72). Received into OPERATING or TRUST; card only into OPERATING. The Stripe payment intent id and the
/// idempotency key are each unique in the firm, so a double click or a repeated webhook records one payment. Money into
/// trust only with trust on, and with its DEPOSIT entry in the same transaction. Insert-only but for the cheque's one
/// "Cleared" tick (AG-6-63 rule 7).
model MoneyPayment {
  id                    String             @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId                String             @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId             String?            @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  trustRequestId        String?            @map("trust_request_id") @db.Uuid
  method                MoneyPaymentMethod
  amountMinor           Int                @map("amount_minor")
  currency              MoneyCurrency
  receivedInto          MoneyAccountKind   @map("received_into")
  receivedAt            DateTime           @map("received_at") @db.Timestamptz
  reference             String?
  /// The optional evidence file of a deposit (a bank slip, a cheque image): a FilesPort key, never the file (FO-7t).
  evidenceFileKey       String?            @map("evidence_file_key")
  stripePaymentIntentId String?            @map("stripe_payment_intent_id")
  idempotencyKey        String             @map("idempotency_key")
  recordedBy            String?            @map("recorded_by")
  cleared               Boolean            @default(true)
  clearedAt             DateTime?          @map("cleared_at") @db.Timestamptz
  clearedBy             String?            @map("cleared_by")
  createdAt             DateTime           @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings     MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  invoice      MoneyInvoice?        @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  trustRequest MoneyTrustRequest?   @relation(fields: [firmId, trustRequestId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  refunds      MoneyRefund[]
  receipt      MoneyReceipt?
  trustEntry   MoneyTrustEntry?
  creditEntries MoneyCreditEntry[]

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@unique([firmId, stripePaymentIntentId])
  @@unique([firmId, idempotencyKey])
  @@index([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@index([firmId, trustRequestId])
  @@map("money_payment")
}

/// A refund of a payment (AG-6-23): an amount, a reason, by card or offline, with its own idempotency key. Refunds of
/// one payment never exceed it, also at REPEATABLE READ (refund_ordinal). Money received into trust goes back as a
/// trust entry instead. Insert-only.
model MoneyRefund {
  id             String           @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId         String           @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  paymentId      String           @map("payment_id") @db.Uuid
  amountMinor    Int              @map("amount_minor")
  currency       MoneyCurrency
  reason         String
  route          MoneyRefundRoute
  stripeRefundId String?          @map("stripe_refund_id")
  idempotencyKey String           @map("idempotency_key")
  /// The database's: the count of the payment's earlier refunds + 1, unique per payment (serialises refunds at any isolation).
  refundOrdinal  Int              @default(0) @map("refund_ordinal")
  createdBy      String           @map("created_by")
  createdAt      DateTime         @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  payment MoneyPayment @relation(fields: [firmId, paymentId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, idempotencyKey])
  @@unique([firmId, stripeRefundId])
  @@unique([firmId, paymentId, refundOrdinal])
  @@index([firmId, paymentId])
  @@map("money_refund")
}

/// A receipt (AG-6-63): one R- series for payment receipts (naming a payment) and trust receipts (naming a deposit
/// entry); at most one receipt per payment and per entry; numbered by the database when written. Never changed.
model MoneyReceipt {
  id           String           @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId       String           @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Always set, by the database when the row is written (a check refuses null); optional here so callers never pass it.
  number       String?
  kind         MoneyReceiptKind
  paymentId    String?          @map("payment_id") @db.Uuid
  trustEntryId String?          @map("trust_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  issuedAt     DateTime         @default(now()) @map("issued_at") @db.Timestamptz

  payment    MoneyPayment?    @relation(fields: [firmId, paymentId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  trustEntry MoneyTrustEntry? @relation(fields: [firmId, trustEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, number])
  @@unique([firmId, paymentId])
  @@unique([firmId, trustEntryId])
  @@map("money_receipt")
}

/// A trust request (AG-6-61, -62; contracts §7 §2.5): money asked of the client to hold in trust, paid straight into the
/// firm's trust bank account, never by card. Its DR- number is taken when it is sent; once sent its party, currency and
/// number never change; a cancel keeps the number and needs a reason. Status is derived from facts (FO-7t).
model MoneyTrustRequest {
  id           String        @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId       String        @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  number       String?
  personId     String?       @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId    String?       @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  caseId       String?       @map("case_id") @db.Uuid
  amountMinor  Int           @map("amount_minor")
  currency     MoneyCurrency @default(CAD)
  purpose      String
  createdBy    String        @map("created_by")
  createdAt    DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz
  sentAt       DateTime?     @map("sent_at") @db.Timestamptz
  sentBy       String?       @map("sent_by")
  cancelledAt  DateTime?     @map("cancelled_at") @db.Timestamptz
  cancelledBy  String?       @map("cancelled_by")
  cancelReason String?       @map("cancel_reason")
  updatedAt    DateTime      @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz
  /// The front office's retainer version a deposit request is for (AG-6-61 rule 7, §7): one request per version (a
  /// partial unique index, in SQL; a cancelled request keeps it); fixed once sent. No key across the module wall.
  retainerVersionId String?    @map("retainer_version_id") @db.Uuid
  /// As on an invoice; unused in R1: no pay link on a trust request (P-567 (3)).
  payLinkTokenHash  String?    @map("pay_link_token_hash")

  settings     MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  payments     MoneyPayment[]
  trustEntries MoneyTrustEntry[]

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@unique([firmId, number])
  @@index([firmId, personId])
  @@index([firmId, companyId])
  @@map("money_trust_request")
}

/// One entry of a party's trust ledger (contracts §7 §2.5; Code s. 32(d): separate records per client). Insert-only.
/// seq and balance_after_minor are the database's: the running balance per (party, currency), which never goes below
/// zero. A withdrawal names an issued invoice of the same party and currency (s. 32(f)); a deposit names the payment
/// received into trust that brought it; a correction names exactly one withdrawal or deposit (never a correction, so
/// it never re-opens an invoice's trust cap, P-603); a refund to the client and a correction carry a reason.
model MoneyTrustEntry {
  id                String              @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId            String              @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  personId          String?             @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId         String?             @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  caseId            String?             @map("case_id") @db.Uuid
  kind              MoneyTrustEntryKind
  amountMinor       Int                 @map("amount_minor")
  currency          MoneyCurrency
  /// seq and balance_after_minor are always the database's (a value the caller gives is replaced).
  seq               Int                 @default(0)
  balanceAfterMinor Int                 @default(0) @map("balance_after_minor")
  invoiceId         String?             @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  paymentId         String?             @map("payment_id") @db.Uuid
  trustRequestId    String?             @map("trust_request_id") @db.Uuid
  correctsEntryId   String?             @map("corrects_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  /// Why a deposit was corrected (FO-7mv): required on a correction of a deposit, null on every other entry.
  correctionKind    MoneyCorrectionKind? @map("correction_kind")
  /// The + half of a move to a case names its − half (FO-7ts part 2); null on every other entry.
  movedFromEntryId  String?             @map("moved_from_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  /// A trust refund's offline details (AG-6-23 rule 2, FO-7ts part 3): required on REFUND_TO_CLIENT (never CARD or
  /// CARD_TERMINAL), null on every other entry.
  refundMethod      MoneyPaymentMethod? @map("refund_method")
  refundedOn        DateTime?           @map("refunded_on") @db.Date
  refundReference   String?             @map("refund_reference")
  /// The refund's payee (AG-6-23 rule 3): none = the entry's party; another payee needs payee_reason.
  payeePersonId     String?             @map("payee_person_id") @db.Uuid
  payeeCompanyId    String?             @map("payee_company_id") @db.Uuid
  payeeName         String?             @map("payee_name")
  payeeReason       String?             @map("payee_reason")
  /// Another payer's money picked for an invoice on the same case (AG-6-68 rule 4; Lead 61): by the writer, with a
  /// reason, at the database's time; all three or none, on WITHDRAWAL_TO_INVOICE only.
  pickedOtherFundsBy     String?        @map("picked_other_funds_by")
  pickedOtherFundsAt     DateTime?      @map("picked_other_funds_at") @db.Timestamptz
  pickedOtherFundsReason String?        @map("picked_other_funds_reason")
  reason            String?
  createdBy         String              @map("created_by")
  createdAt         DateTime            @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings     MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  invoice      MoneyInvoice?        @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  payment      MoneyPayment?        @relation(fields: [firmId, paymentId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  trustRequest MoneyTrustRequest?   @relation(fields: [firmId, trustRequestId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  corrects     MoneyTrustEntry?     @relation("MoneyTrustCorrection", fields: [firmId, correctsEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  correctedBy  MoneyTrustEntry[]    @relation("MoneyTrustCorrection")
  movedFrom    MoneyTrustEntry?     @relation("MoneyTrustMove", fields: [firmId, movedFromEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  movedTo      MoneyTrustEntry[]    @relation("MoneyTrustMove")
  receipt      MoneyReceipt?
  moveLines    MoneyMoveLine[]
  overpaidCreditNotes MoneyCreditNote[] @relation("MoneyCreditNoteOverpaid")

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@unique([firmId, personId, currency, seq])
  @@unique([firmId, companyId, currency, seq])
  @@unique([firmId, paymentId])
  @@index([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@index([firmId, caseId])
  @@index([firmId, correctsEntryId])
  @@unique([firmId, movedFromEntryId])
  @@map("money_trust_entry")
}

/// A party's tax treatment (AG-6-4 rule 2 §7; FO-7ts part 3): one row per party; no row = Taxable.
model MoneyPartyTaxTreatment {
  id        String            @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId    String            @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  personId  String?           @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId String?           @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  treatment MoneyTaxTreatment
  updatedBy String            @map("updated_by")
  updatedAt DateTime          @default(now()) @updatedAt @map("updated_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, personId])
  @@unique([firmId, companyId])
  @@map("money_party_tax_treatment")
}

/// One entry of a holder's credit ledger (FO-7ts part 2; AG-6-21 rules 2-3, 5 §7 CreditEntry; AG-6-23 rules 1, 4). The
/// holder is the case, or the party when there is no case; the party is on every entry. seq and balance_after_minor are
/// the database's, per holder and currency, never below zero. KEPT names its payment, APPLIED its invoice (same holder
/// and currency, draft or issued), REVERSED the KEPT or APPLIED entry it undoes; REFUNDED and REVERSED carry a reason.
/// Credit is not trust money. Insert-only.
model MoneyCreditEntry {
  id                String          @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId            String          @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  personId          String?         @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId         String?         @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  caseId            String?         @map("case_id") @db.Uuid
  kind              MoneyCreditKind
  amountMinor       Int             @map("amount_minor")
  currency          MoneyCurrency
  seq               Int             @default(0)
  balanceAfterMinor Int             @default(0) @map("balance_after_minor")
  paymentId         String?         @map("payment_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId         String?         @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  reversesEntryId   String?         @map("reverses_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  reason            String?
  createdBy         String          @map("created_by")
  createdAt         DateTime        @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings   MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  payment    MoneyPayment?        @relation(fields: [firmId, paymentId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  invoice    MoneyInvoice?        @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  reverses   MoneyCreditEntry?    @relation("MoneyCreditReversal", fields: [firmId, reversesEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  reversedBy MoneyCreditEntry[]   @relation("MoneyCreditReversal")

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@index([firmId, paymentId])
  @@index([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@index([firmId, reversesEntryId])
  @@map("money_credit_entry")
}

/// A write-off of an issued invoice's small balance (AG-6-76): amount, reason (1-200 characters), by, at. At most one per
/// invoice; never on a draft; insert-only.
model MoneyWriteOff {
  id          String        @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId      String        @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId   String        @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  amountMinor Int           @map("amount_minor")
  currency    MoneyCurrency
  reason      String
  createdBy   String        @map("created_by")
  createdAt   DateTime      @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  invoice MoneyInvoice @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@map("money_write_off")
}

/// "I moved these" (AG-6-73 rule 3; FO-7mv): one batch of bank transfers between trust and operating, in one currency
/// and one direction, with the transfer date (the firm's bank step, a date with no zone) and who recorded it; the time
/// is the database's. ExpatReady moves no money. Never changed (rule 6): a mistake is undone by an undo batch that names
/// the batch it undoes and a reason (its lines go back to the list); one undo per batch; an undo is never undone and
/// carries no lines. Insert-only.
model MoneyMoveBatch {
  id            String             @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId        String             @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  currency      MoneyCurrency
  direction     MoneyMoveDirection
  transferDate  DateTime?          @map("transfer_date") @db.Date
  undoesBatchId String?            @map("undoes_batch_id") @db.Uuid
  reason        String?
  recordedBy    String             @map("recorded_by")
  recordedAt    DateTime           @default(now()) @map("recorded_at") @db.Timestamptz

  settings MoneyPaymentSettings @relation(fields: [firmId], references: [firmId], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  undoes   MoneyMoveBatch?      @relation("MoneyMoveUndo", fields: [firmId, undoesBatchId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  undoneBy MoneyMoveBatch?      @relation("MoneyMoveUndo")
  lines    MoneyMoveLine[]

  @@unique([firmId, id])
  @@unique([firmId, undoesBatchId])
  @@map("money_move_batch")
}

/// One moved amount in a batch (AG-6-73 rule 1; FO-7mv): its kind, the batch's currency and direction, the amount and
/// the trust entry it moves (a WITHDRAWAL_TO_INVOICE for TRUST_APPLIED; a WRONG_ACCOUNT correction of a deposit for
/// WRONG_ACCOUNT); the invoice and party are copied from that entry by the database. The moves of one entry, net of
/// undone batches, never exceed what it still holds (B-18, B-19); move_ordinal (the database's) is unique per entry, so
/// two writers at once make one move. Lines are written in the transaction that records their batch, never after its
/// undo. Insert-only.
model MoneyMoveLine {
  id            String             @id @default(dbgenerated("gen_random_uuid()")) @db.Uuid
  firmId        String             @map("firm_id") @db.Uuid
  batchId       String             @map("batch_id") @db.Uuid
  kind          MoneyMoveKind
  direction     MoneyMoveDirection
  currency      MoneyCurrency
  amountMinor   Int                @map("amount_minor")
  sourceEntryId String             @map("source_entry_id") @db.Uuid
  invoiceId     String?            @map("invoice_id") @db.Uuid
  personId      String?            @map("person_id") @db.Uuid
  companyId     String?            @map("company_id") @db.Uuid
  /// The database's (a value the caller gives is replaced).
  moveOrdinal   Int                @default(0) @map("move_ordinal")
  createdAt     DateTime           @default(now()) @map("created_at") @db.Timestamptz

  batch       MoneyMoveBatch  @relation(fields: [firmId, batchId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  sourceEntry MoneyTrustEntry @relation(fields: [firmId, sourceEntryId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)
  invoice     MoneyInvoice?   @relation(fields: [firmId, invoiceId], references: [firmId, id], onDelete: Restrict, onUpdate: Restrict)

  @@unique([firmId, sourceEntryId, moveOrdinal])
  @@index([firmId, batchId])
  @@index([firmId, invoiceId])
  @@map("money_move_line")
}
